## Answer

**Yes**, $1093^2 \mid 2^{1093} - 2$.

### Proof

We show $2^{1092} \equiv 1 \pmod{1093^2}$ (i.e., 1093 is a Wieferich prime). Then $2^{1093} = 2\cdot 2^{1092} \equiv 2 \pmod{1093^2}$, giving the result.

Set $M = 1093^2 = 1{,}194{,}649$. We compute $2^{2^k} \pmod M$ by repeated squaring, writing each residue as $a + b\cdot 1093$.

| $k$ | $2^{2^k} \equiv a_k + b_k\cdot 1093 \pmod M$ |
|-----|---------------------------------------------|
| 0 | $2$ |
| 1 | $4$ |
| 2 | $16$ |
| 3 | $256$ |
| 4 | $1049 + 59\cdot 1093$ |
| 5 | $843 + 186\cdot 1093$ |
| 6 | $199 + 555\cdot 1093$ |
| 7 | $253 + 140\cdot 1093$ |
| 8 | $615 + 946\cdot 1093$ |
| 9 | $47 + 974\cdot 1093$ |
| 10 | $23 + 839\cdot 1093$ |

**Sample squaring step** (the rest are identical in form): from $2^{512} \equiv 47 + 974\cdot 1093$,
$$2^{1024} \equiv 47^2 + 2\cdot 47\cdot 974\cdot 1093 \pmod M.$$
$47^2 = 2209 = 23 + 2\cdot 1093$; $\;2\cdot 47\cdot 974 = 91556 = 837 + 83\cdot 1093$. Hence
$$2^{1024} \equiv (23+2\cdot 1093) + (837+83\cdot 1093)\cdot 1093 \equiv 23 + 839\cdot 1093 \pmod M.$$

**Combining.** Since $1092 = 1024 + 64 + 4$:
$$2^{1092} = 2^{1024}\cdot 2^{64}\cdot 2^{4}.$$

First, $2^{1024}\cdot 2^{64}$: with $2^{1024}\equiv 23+839\cdot 1093$ and $2^{64}\equiv 199+555\cdot 1093$,
$$23\cdot 199 = 4577 = 205 + 4\cdot 1093,$$
$$23\cdot 555 + 839\cdot 199 = 12765 + 166961 = 179726 = 474 + 164\cdot 1093.$$
So
$$2^{1088} \equiv 205 + (4+474)\cdot 1093 = 205 + 478\cdot 1093 \pmod M.$$

Finally multiply by $2^4 = 16$:
$$2^{1092} \equiv 16(205 + 478\cdot 1093) = 3280 + 7648\cdot 1093 \pmod M.$$
$$3280 = 1 + 3\cdot 1093, \qquad 7648 = -3 + 7\cdot 1093.$$
Therefore
$$2^{1092} \equiv (1+3\cdot 1093) + (-3+7\cdot 1093)\cdot 1093 = 1 + 3\cdot 1093 - 3\cdot 1093 + 7\cdot 1093^2 \equiv 1 \pmod{1093^2}.$$

The critical cancellation $3\cdot 1093 - 3\cdot 1093 = 0$ yields exactly
$$\boxed{2^{1092} \equiv 1 \pmod{1093^2}}.$$

Consequently
$$2^{1093} - 2 = 2(2^{1092}-1) \equiv 2\cdot 0 = 0 \pmod{1093^2},$$
so $1093^2 \mid 2^{1093}-2$. $\blacksquare$

